
# Universal House Price Prediction System

An end-to-end Machine Learning project that predicts residential
house prices using regression algorithms, automated preprocessing,
hyperparameter optimization, and model evaluation.

Developed as part of the Codveda Technologies Data Science Internship.

## Project Overview

This project uses the Ames Housing dataset to develop a reusable
house price prediction workflow.

The system performs:

- Data inspection and exploratory data analysis.
- Missing-value investigation and preprocessing.
- Numerical and categorical feature transformation.
- Regression model training and comparison.
- Hyperparameter tuning using cross-validation.
- Model diagnostics and feature importance analysis.
- Final model training and prediction on unseen housing data.

**Important:** The current implementation is configured for the
Ames Housing dataset. The preprocessing architecture is reusable,
but other datasets may require their own feature mappings,
missing-value rules, and model retraining.

## Dataset

Source: Kaggle - House Prices: Advanced Regression Techniques

https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/house-prices-advanced-regression-techniques/data

| Dataset | Records | Description |
|---|---:|---|
| train.csv | 1,460 | Housing features and SalePrice |
| test.csv | 1,459 | Housing features without SalePrice |
| data_description.txt | - | Feature descriptions |
| sample_submission.csv | 1,459 | Kaggle submission format |

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas and NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Scikit-learn
- SciPy
- Joblib
- VS Code

## Machine Learning Algorithms

Three regression algorithms were implemented:

1. Linear Regression
2. Decision Tree Regression
3. Random Forest Regression

Model optimization was performed using RandomizedSearchCV
with 5-fold cross-validation.

